    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Anthropic blocks users for anything touching training larger models",
      "url": "https://twitter.com/jiahaoshao1/status/2116475922190922088",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50319358",
      "score": 459,
      "comments": 256,
      "author": "pretext",
      "published": "2026-10-31T19:39:19Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Anthropic aggressively enforces terms of service, banning API accounts that use Claude outputs for synthetic data generation or model distillation.",
        "Distillation pipelines leveraging Claude 3.5 Sonnet face immediate disruption, exposing severe vendor lock-in and operational risks for AI builders.",
        "Strict non-compete clauses in proprietary LLM APIs are accelerating developer migration to open-weight models like Llama 3 for training data."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "Avoid Public Functions Calling Other Public Functions",
      "url": "https://matklad.github.io/2026/10/29/pub-calls-pub.html",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/k508we",
      "score": 90,
      "comments": 20,
      "author": "telemachus",
      "published": "2026-10-31T18:05:03Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Chaining public methods internally couples API contracts and frequently triggers redundant input validation or unexpected state transitions.",
        "Delegate shared logic to private helper functions, keeping public interfaces as thin orchestration layers over reusable internal implementations.",
        "Internal public calls harm extensibility in object-oriented systems, causing fragile base classes and making mocking or overriding unpredictable."
      ]
    },
